    <briefdescription>
<para>Ukrainian calendars. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Holidays for the Ukrainian stock exchange (data from <ulink url="http://www.ukrse.kiev.ua/eng/">http://www.ukrse.kiev.ua/eng/</ulink>): <itemizedlist>
<listitem>
<para>Saturdays </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Sundays </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>New Year&apos;s Day, January 1st </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Orthodox Christmas, January 7th </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>International Women&apos;s Day, March 8th </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Easter Monday </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Holy Trinity Day, 50 days after Easter </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>International Workers&apos; Solidarity Days, May 1st and 2nd </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Victory Day, May 9th </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Constitution Day, June 28th </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Independence Day, August 24th </para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
Holidays falling on a Saturday or Sunday are moved to the following Monday. </para>    </detaileddescription>
